    {
      "claim": "L4 shows that the query's closest structural relatives are orally absorbable amino-beta-lactams: amoxicillin (same p-hydroxy phenylglycine side chain) has high aqueous solubility (4.4–7.69 mg/mL at pH 1.2–6.8), and cephalexin (same cephalosporin core) has measurable Caco-2 permeability (8.42×10^-7 cm/s at apical pH 6.0). This supports carrier-mediated intestinal absorption for the query despite its low passive permeability.",
      "card_ids": ["C52","C53","C57","C58","C59","C63"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The low-permeability records (amoxicillin PAMPA no permeation; piperacillin Caco-2 3.25×10^-8 to 3.22×10^-7 cm/s; cephalexin zero in one mixture condition at apical pH 7.4) are not affirmative evidence for F < 20%: amino-beta-lactams are absorbed by PEPT1-type transporters, and piperacillin lacks the α-amino phenylglycine motif present in the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C55","C56","C60","C61","C62"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral Cmax records for oral beta-lactams (S-1090 2.01–6.10 µg/mL at 50–400 mg; ampicillin 9.53 µg/mL after 500 mg sultamicillin; amoxicillin 11.4 µg/mL after 200 mg in dogs; cefpodoxime proxetil 1.32 mg/L after 100 mg) demonstrate measurable systemic exposure after oral dosing in this structural class.",
      "card_ids": ["C40","C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "All transferable numeric absolute-bioavailability contexts in L1/L2 are >=23% (e.g., maraviroc 23–33%, indinavir 40–65%, ezetimibe 35–60%, garenoxacin 92%, DPP-4 inhibitors 75–87%, ciprofibrate ~90%, levodopa 71–86%); no supplied record affirmatively supports F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C07","C10","C11","C13","C15","C16","C18","C20","C21","C22","C25","C28","C30","C31","C37","C38"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "high",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C52","C53","C57","C58","C59","C63"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query or an exact cefatrizine context is supplied.",
    "L3 provides Cmax only, without IV-comparator AUC or F; L4 is in vitro and not a systemic-F measurement.",
    "No PEPT1-specific uptake assay for the query; carrier-mediated absorption is inferred from structure and class behavior.",
    "Fasted-state in vivo PK for the query is not directly measured; L3 records are nonfasting or unspecified.",
    "Dose, formulation, and first-pass/hepatic clearance for the query are unknown."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L4 adds class-relevant solubility and permeability evidence: amoxicillin is highly soluble and cephalexin shows measurable Caco-2 permeability, while low passive-permeability records are mechanistically expected for amino-beta-lactams and do not support F < 20%. Combined with L3 oral Cmax for oral beta-lactams and the absence of any affirmative low-F record, F >= 20% is better supported. Prediction remains high and is strengthened."
}

